  "description": "QOSJUD crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C40 H54 N8 O25 Tb4. From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb1B (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2B (Tb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.389-5.295 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.34-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C40H54N8O25Tb4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
